From: ATOMiK Project
Subject: [PATCH] usb: phy: allow USB_ULPI on RISC-V

The USB_ULPI driver depends on `ARM || ARM64 || COMPILE_TEST`. The
generic ULPI PHY driver (`drivers/usb/phy/phy-ulpi.c`) is architecture-
independent — it only writes to a memory-mapped viewport register on
the host controller. There's no reason it can't be enabled on RISC-V,
which is required for ChipIdea-based USB host controllers reached via
GP1/GP0 AXI masters from soft RV64 cores (e.g. our NaxRiscv on Zynq-7020).

Without this, `compatible = "ulpi-phy"` device-tree nodes have no driver
to bind, the kernel falls back to `usb-nop-xceiv` semantics, and the
ULPI viewport never gets the DrvVbusExternal write — so the on-board
TPS2051 5V switch stays off and every HID enumeration times out at -110.

Apply with:
    cd hardware/zynq/litex-build/linux-build/litex-linux
    patch -p1 < ../../scripts/kernel_patches/0001-usb-phy-allow-USB_ULPI-on-RISCV.patch

---
 drivers/usb/phy/Kconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/phy/Kconfig b/drivers/usb/phy/Kconfig
--- a/drivers/usb/phy/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/usb/phy/Kconfig
@@ -173,7 +173,7 @@ config USB_TEGRA_PHY

 config USB_ULPI
 	bool "Generic ULPI Transceiver Driver"
-	depends on ARM || ARM64 || COMPILE_TEST
+	depends on ARM || ARM64 || RISCV || COMPILE_TEST
 	select USB_ULPI_VIEWPORT
 	help
 	  Enable this to support ULPI connected USB OTG transceivers which
